$ A-B regular solution
$ Written by phase-diagram-explorer 0.2.0.
$ Synthetic test fixture: tests/fixtures/regular_solution.json exported with write_tdb.
$ Source: Synthetic symmetric regular solution for validating miscibility gap
$ handling: one solution phase with ideal end members (G = 0) and a single
$ Redlich-Kister parameter L0 = 20000 J/mol, so the gap is symmetric about x =
$ 0.5 with critical temperature Tc = L0 / (2R) = 1202.73 K and binodal
$ ln(x/(1-x)) = L0(2x-1)/(RT).
$
ELEMENT /-   ELECTRON_GAS  0.0 0.0 0.0 !
ELEMENT VA   VACUUM        0.0 0.0 0.0 !
ELEMENT A ALPHA 50.0 0.0 0.0 !
ELEMENT B ALPHA 100.0 0.0 0.0 !

TYPE_DEFINITION % SEQ * !
DEFINE_SYSTEM_DEFAULT ELEMENT 2 !
DEFAULT_COMMAND DEF_SYS_ELEMENT VA /- !

PHASE ALPHA % 1 1.0 !
CONSTITUENT ALPHA :A,B: !
PARAMETER G(ALPHA,A;0) 1.0 0.0; 10000.0 N !
PARAMETER G(ALPHA,B;0) 1.0 0.0; 10000.0 N !
PARAMETER L(ALPHA,A,B;0) 1.0 20000.0; 10000.0 N !
